<p id="S2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The Hessian
bound in part (i) follows immediately from (<a href="#S1.E1" title="Equation 1.1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>); the
Poincaré and covariance bounds then follow from the standard
log-concavity facts (<a href="#A4.E6" title="Equation D.6 ‣ D.2 Strong log-concavity and covariance bounds ‣ Appendix D Technical tools ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.6</span></a>) and
<a href="#A4.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma D.3 (Two-sided covariance bound). ‣ D.2 Strong log-concavity and covariance bounds ‣ Appendix D Technical tools ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a> in Appendix <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Technical tools ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>, applied with
<math id="S2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=\alpha+\eta^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=\alpha+\eta^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=\beta+\eta^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=\beta+\eta^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. The
marginal curvature bound in part (ii) is derived in
Appendix <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Technical tools ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>, at (<a href="#A4.E10" title="Equation D.10 ‣ Hessian of the augmented marginal. ‣ D.2 Strong log-concavity and covariance bounds ‣ Appendix D Technical tools ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.10</span></a>). The
reflection statement follows directly from (<a href="#S2.E6" title="Equation 2.6 ‣ 2.2 Proximal augmentation and the restricted Gaussian oracle ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.6</span></a>).</p>